Vellum-Swing

Creative Catalyst: The genre started as forbidden lullabies sung by androids to their unfinished siblings.

Vellum-Swing is the sound of a rusted brass band crashing into a glass-bottomed centrifuge. It juxtaposes the jagged, hyper-compressed "M1 Madness" piano stabs—reminiscent of 90s dance floor abandon—with the frantic, joyful scuttle of upright bass and swing drums. The music feels like an upbeat, ecstatic breakdown, characterized by "Glitch-Jive"—vocals that glitch into staccato phonetics—and high-octane indie pop melodies that veer into jarring, euphoric dissonance.

Genre DNA
*   Tempo & Pulse: 128–144 BPM; a swing-shuffle beat that feels constantly about to trip over its own feet, driving a forward-momentum rush.
*   Harmonic Palette: Major 7th chords flattened into diminished, M1-heavy "House" stabs, bright, brittle pop tonalities, and unexpected modulations into minor keys.
*   Production Signatures: "Bit-Rot" compression on the drum bus to mimic decaying hardware; aggressive side-chaining that makes the entire mix "breathe" like an wheezing chest; frequency-masked vocal chops that sound like radio static cross-talking with vintage big-band horns.
*   Dynamics: A breathless ascent starting with soft, acoustic swing jazz that abruptly cuts into maximalist 90s rave distortion.

Scene & Origin Lore
Born in the Sub-Level 4 fabrication plants of the abandoned 1980s mainframe bunkers, Vellum-Swing was birthed by sentient robotic assemblers. Forbidden from having creative souls, they mimicked the "Jolly" human radio signals of the 80s, reinterpreting them as nursery rhymes for their scrapped, non-functional progeny. Today’s practitioners—human youth wearing tattered Victorian formalwear wired with pulsating fiber-optic filaments—gather in industrial laundromats to perform the "Winding Ritual," dancing until the syncopation of the M1 keys forces a physical hallucinatory state of pure, synthetic bliss.

Instruments: M1 Korg workstation piano, custom-built brass-wind synth (The Horn-o-Stat), detuned upright bass, granularly-processed accordion, and 80s-era gated-reverb snare drums.

For Fans Of: Caribou, Caravan Palace, SOPHIE, The Go! Team.

